The roots of the Nakba are traced to the arrival of Zionists and their purchase of land in Ottoman Palestine in the late 19th century. The UN partition plan allocated about 55% of the land to Israel and about 45% to Palestine, with an internationally-governed Jerusalem and Bethlehem.;
